  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Exploded View\n\nAn isometric stack of slabs springs apart with leader lines and labels, holds, then clicks back together.\n\nCategory: camera. Length: 2.333 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- An architecture or a product stack should be explained layer by layer, such as interface, engine, storage and hardware.\n- One layer of a system is the point of the story and should be called out in brand color.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The object should turn to show its front and back rather than come apart: use turntable.\n- The layers are numbers to compare rather than parts of one thing: use animated-bar-chart.\n\nVariables:\n- layers (number, 2-6): Layers, default 4\n- labels (string): Labels, default \"Interface, Engine, Storage, Hardware\"\n- highlight (number, 0-5): Highlight, default 1\n- background_color (color): Background, default \"#111111\"\n- top_color (color): Top face, default \"#F4F4F4\"\n- left_color (color): Left face, default \"#A6A6A6\"\n- right_color (color): Right face, default \"#747474\"\n- highlight_top_color (color): Highlight top, default \"#E5322D\"\n- highlight_left_color (color): Highlight left, default \"#B5231F\"\n- highlight_right_color (color): Highlight right, default \"#8A1A17\"\n- line_color (color): Leader lines, default \"#FFFFFF\"\n- label_color (color): Labels, default \"#FFFFFF\"\n- speed (number, 0.25-3): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
